The `createArchiveOutputStream` method in `ArchiveStreamFactory` is responsible for creating `ArchiveOutputStream` instances based on the provided archiver name and output stream. Here is a snippet of the method:

```java
     public ArchiveOutputStream createArchiveOutputStream(
             final String archiverName, final OutputStream out)
             throws ArchiveException {
         if (archiverName == null || out == null) {
             throw new IllegalArgumentException(
                     "Archivername and stream must not be null.");
         }

         if ("ar".equalsIgnoreCase(archiverName)) {
             return new ArArchiveOutputStream(out);
         } else if ("zip".equalsIgnoreCase(archiverName)) {
             return new ZipArchiveOutputStream(out);
         } else if ("tar".equalsIgnoreCase(archiverName)) {
             return new TarArchiveOutputStream(out);
         } else if ("jar".equalsIgnoreCase(archiverName)) {
             return new JarArchiveOutputStream(out);
         } else if ("cpio".equalsIgnoreCase(archiverName)) {
             return new CpioArchiveOutputStream(out);
         }
         throw new ArchiveException("Archiver: " + archiverName + " not found.");
     }
```

This method selects the appropriate concrete subclass of `ArchiveOutputStream` based on the archiver name and creates an instance with the provided output stream.

